From 433316d68a6fd3cf43aabe6d76cdf55540f2467b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kerfand <Kerfand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:39:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fuxi: arm64e xnu-10063 kernel for the iOS 17.7 21H16
 kernelcache

Checkpoint 1 of the iPhone15,2 iOS 17.7 move: an arm64e xnu-10063 kernel
prelinked with the original 21H16 fileset kexts boots on fuxi to the
root-device wait (fastboot boot only).

- patches/xnu-10063-arm64e: native PAC keys, threaded starts, upstream clang
  __ptrauth form, the fileset unmapped-call stub with the unixnu-unmapped
  probe (logs site, x0-x3, x16), keeping a split 2 MB block's mapping on the
  4K-page kernel, signing the early security initializer before the call,
  and the IIG StateNotificationItemCreate handler without a member function
  pointer cast.
- scripts: kernel and cc_kext slices follow UNIXNU_XNU_ARCH; arm64e adds the
  function pointer type discrimination Apple clang uses for -mkernel.
- kits/XnuPrelink: 21H16 fileset support and reviewed identities.
- .gitignore: the out-ios17 output root.
